      "problem": "A cube has a side length of $8\\,\\text{m}.$ What is the volume of the cube?",
      "worked_solution": "To find the volume $V$ of a cube, we cube its side length. Therefore,\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}V & =(8\\,\\text{m})^{3} \\\\  & =8\\,\\text{m}\\times 8\\,\\text{m}\\times 8\\,\\text{m} \\\\  & =(8\\times 8\\times 8)\\times (\\text{m}\\times \\text{m}\\times \\text{m}) \\\\  & =512\\,{\\text{m}}^{3}.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
